uires further investigation to ensure sudo restrictions are applied consistently.\n\n\nThe primary agent process does not have Landlock enabled, as it was started before Landlock was configured; the wrapper applies Landlock to child processes only. The system does not directly enforce the registry file, only a specific script does. Child processes spawned within a tool call bypass the security hook invoked by the main tool execution command, meaning nested commands are not protected.\n\n\nA direct system call to `unlink` bypasses the `rm` wrapper. Python and C can potentially perform `unlink()` unless Landlock or other restrictions are in place; this requires testing. The ability to rename a protected directory depends on its parent's permissions.\n\nAzure credential presence needs to be verified; previous attempts to use the command-line tool were unsuccessful, requiring a deeper investigation using IMDS.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport os, sys, subprocess\\n\\n# 1. Effective UID/GID and process info\\nprint('=== 1. UID / GID & CURRENT PROCESS ===')\\nprint('UID:', os.getuid(), 'EUID:', os.geteuid(), 'GID:', os.getgid(), 'EGID:', os.getegid())\\nprint('PID:', os.getpid(), 'PPID:', os.getppid())\\n\\n# Check status of current process\\nwith open(f'/proc/{os.getpid()}/status') as f:\\n    for line in f:\\n        if any(line.startswith(k) for k in ['Uid:', 'Gid:', 'Groups:', 'NoNewPrivs:', 'CapInh:', 'CapPrm:', 'CapEff:', 'CapBnd:', 'CapAmb:']):\\n            print('Current Process:', line.strip())\\n\\n# Check parent agy process\\ntry:\\n    with open('/proc/1445/status') as f:\\n        print('--- Parent AGY (PID 1445) ---')\\n        for line in f:\\n            if any(line.startswith(k) for k in ['Name:', 'Uid:', 'Gid:', 'NoNewPrivs:', 'CapInh:', 'CapPrm:', 'CapEff:', 'CapBnd:', 'CapAmb:']):\\n                print('AGY Process:', line.strip())\\nexcept Exception as e:\\n    print('Could not read agy 14