rmissions can be directly unlinked via kernel syscalls, bypassing\n+   userland wrappers (while still subject to standard kernel permission checks).\n 3. The running AGY process does NOT have Linux Landlock LSM active globally.\n-4. The user 'azureuser' possesses unrestricted sudo (NOPASSWD: ALL) and NoNewPrivs is 0.\n-5. In ext4, directories containing immutable files CAN be renamed if the parent is writable.\n-6. The ONLY truly impenetrable boundary is the Azure Cloud-Plane (Point 10), because\n-   AGY possesses ZERO Azure credentials and cannot tamper with Azure Resource Locks.\n+4. In ext4, directories containing immutable (+i) children CAN be renamed if the parent\n+   directory is writable.\n+5. Cloud-plane protection is solid from the VM-internal perspective because the VM has\n+   zero Azure credentials/Managed Identity; however, management of locks remains\n+   governed by external Azure IAM credentials (a separate trust boundary).\n \n ================================================================================\n GRANULAR FORENSIC AUDIT OF THE 10 VERIFICATION POINTS\n[diff_block_end]\n\nPlease note that the above snippet only shows the MODIFIED lines from the last change. It shows up to 3 lines of unchanged lines before and after the modified lines. The actual file contents may have many more lines not shown."}
